Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `mbb_pbp_sr.season` – filter events to the seasons 2010‑2018 inclusive.  
• `mbb_pbp_sr.period` – pick only second–period (= 2) plays.  
• `mbb_pbp_sr.points_scored` – number of points credited on each play; will be aggregated.  
• `mbb_pbp_sr.player_id` – allows us to count distinct players.  
• `mbb_pbp_sr.team_market` – the school (e.g. “Duke”); used to rank markets.  
• `mbb_pbp_sr.game_id` – needed when summing a player’s second‑period points inside one game.  

• `mbb_historical_tournament_games.season` – filter tournament games to 2010‑2018.  
• `…round` – tournament round (64, 32, Sweet 16, etc.).  
• `…game_date` – calendar date of the game.  
• `win_market / lose_market` – tells which school was on each side; used to match the top‑five markets.  
• `win_name / lose_name`, `win_seed / lose_seed`, `win_pts / lose_pts` – requested game details.  

Typical conditions  
```
WHERE season BETWEEN 2010 AND 2018
  AND period = 2
  AND points_scored IS NOT NULL
```

--------------------------------------------------------------------
Below are ten exploratory‐to‑final BigQuery SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that walk through the problem, from simple inspection to the final answer.

```sql
-- 1. Seasons available in play‑by‑play data
SELECT DISTINCT season
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
ORDER BY season
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Sample second‑period scoring plays (2010‑2018)
SELECT season, game_id, team_market, player_id,
       period, points_scored, event_description
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
WHERE season BETWEEN 2010 AND 2018
  AND period = 2
  AND points_scored IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Second‑period points by player in a single season (2010)
SELECT season, player_id, team_market,
       SUM(points_scored) AS period2_pts
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
WHERE season = 2010
  AND period = 2
  AND points_scored IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY season, player_id, team_market
HAVING period2_pts >= 15
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Per‑game second‑period totals (needed so a 15‑point game counts)
SELECT season, game_id, player_id, team_market,
       SUM(points_scored) AS period2_pts
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
WHERE season BETWEEN 2010 AND 2018
  AND period = 2
  AND points_scored IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY season, game_id, player_id, team_market
HAVING period2_pts >= 15
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Distinct players per market that ever hit 15+ in a 2nd period (2010‑18)
WITH big_games AS (
  SELECT player_id, team_market
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
  WHERE season BETWEEN 2010 AND 2018
    AND period = 2
    AND points_scored IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY season, game_id, player_id, team_market
  HAVING SUM(points_scored) >= 15
)
SELECT team_market,
       COUNT(DISTINCT player_id) AS distinct_players
FROM big_games
GROUP BY team_market
ORDER BY distinct_players DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Top five markets by that metric
WITH big_games AS (
  SELECT player_id, team_market
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
  WHERE season BETWEEN 2010 AND 2018
    AND period = 2
    AND points_scored IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY season, game_id, player_id, team_market
  HAVING SUM(points_scored) >= 15
)
SELECT team_market,
       COUNT(DISTINCT player_id) AS distinct_players
FROM big_games
GROUP BY team_market
ORDER BY distinct_players DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

```sql
-- 7. Sample tournament games (winner’s side) 2010‑18
SELECT season, round, game_date,
       win_market, win_name, win_seed, win_pts
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_historical_tournament_games`
WHERE season BETWEEN 2010 AND 2018
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Tournament games where “Duke” was involved, 2010‑18
SELECT season, round, game_date,
       win_market, win_name, win_pts,
       lose_market, lose_name, lose_pts
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_historical_tournament_games`
WHERE season BETWEEN 2010 AND 2018
  AND (win_market = 'Duke' OR lose_market = 'Duke')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Join: top‑five markets <> tournament games 2010‑18
WITH top5 AS (
  WITH big_games AS (
    SELECT player_id, team_market
    FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
    WHERE season BETWEEN 2010 AND 2018
      AND period = 2
      AND points_scored IS NOT NULL
    GROUP BY season, game_id, player_id, team_market
    HAVING SUM(points_scored) >= 15
  )
  SELECT team_market
  FROM (
    SELECT team_market,
           COUNT(DISTINCT player_id) AS cnt
    FROM big_games
    GROUP BY team_market
    ORDER BY cnt DESC
    LIMIT 5
  )
)
SELECT t.season, t.round, t.game_date,
       t.win_market, t.win_name, t.win_seed, t.win_pts,
       t.lose_market, t.lose_name, t.lose_seed, t.lose_pts
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_historical_tournament_games` AS t
JOIN top5 ON t.win_market = top5.team_market
          OR t.lose_market = top5.team_market
WHERE t.season BETWEEN 2010 AND 2018
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final answer: every 2010‑18 tournament game for the
--     five markets with the most distinct players who scored
--     15+ in a second period (limit 20 rows for display).
WITH player_big_games AS (
  SELECT season, game_id, player_id, team_market,
         SUM(points_scored) AS period2_pts
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_pbp_sr`
  WHERE season BETWEEN 2010 AND 2018
    AND period = 2
    AND points_scored IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY season, game_id, player_id, team_market
  HAVING period2_pts >= 15
),
top_markets AS (
  SELECT team_market AS market,
         COUNT(DISTINCT player_id) AS num_players
  FROM player_big_games
  GROUP BY team_market
  ORDER BY num_players DESC
  LIMIT 5
),
tourney AS (
  SELECT *
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_historical_tournament_games`
  WHERE season BETWEEN 2010 AND 2018
)
SELECT
  t.season,
  t.round,
  t.game_date,
  t.win_market,
  t.win_name,
  t.win_seed,
  t.win_pts,
  t.lose_market,
  t.lose_name,
  t.lose_seed,
  t.lose_pts
FROM tourney AS t
JOIN top_markets AS m
  ON t.win_market = m.market OR t.lose_market = m.market
ORDER BY t.season, t.game_date
LIMIT 20;
```

The tenth query delivers the requested list of NCAA tournament games (2010‑2018) involving each of the five school markets that produced the greatest number of distinct players who scored at least 15 points in any second period during that same span.
